    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • Project KO11 Is Proof That Geely Wants To \"Knock Out\" Range Rover, Launches Next Year in Europe\nNew Zenos E10 Is a 380-HP British Sports Car That Weighs Less Than a Mazda MX-5 Miata\n6 photos\nPhoto: Zenos\nChances are you may not know that much about Zenos Cars , especially its E10 model, unless you live in the United Kingdom, but the British automaker’s model is now back for 2027.\nWe are talking about a new generation of the Zenos E10, which is the successor to the one made between 2015 and 2016. The original E10 is estimated to have been made in over 100 units, and it is yet unknown how many of the latest will see the light of day, as the company hasn’t announced this detail at the time of writing.\nThe new 2027 Zenos E10 family is said to “ provide high-performance and advanced engineering at a time when new, pure-bred sports cars are increasingly rare. ” And who are we to contradict them? Especially when it comes to the latter part, because these things are almost unicorns in today’s automotive kingdom.\nZenos’ new E10 sports a carbon fiber tub, an extruded aluminum chassis, and benefits from full carbon fiber bodywork. This means that it is on the very lightweight side of things. In fact, the automaker says that it tips the scales at only 1,742 pounds (790 kg). In order to better understand the weight of the 2027 E10, we will remind you that the aging Mazda MX-5 ND, aka the fourth generation, has a curb weight of 2,183 pounds (990 kg) in its base flavor.\nPhoto: Zenos But what powers it? A 2.0-liter four-cylinder engine that pushes out 380 brake horsepower (385 ps/283 kW ) at 6,000 rpm and 376 pound-feet (510 Nm) of torque between 3,000 and 4,500 rpm. This applies to the E10 rZ, and it translates to around 480 brake horsepower (487 ps/353 kW) per metric ton (2,205 lbs). That’s pretty much on par with the iconic Lamborghini Aventador SVJ Roadster , more than the Maserati MC20, and roughly the same as the E10 R (old one).\nIn addition to the rZ version of the new Zenos E10, the company also offers it in the r2 configuration. This model uses a 2.3-liter engine said to deliver 300 hp (304 ps/221 kW) at 6,000 rpm, and 313 pound-feet (425 Nm) of torque at 3,500 rpm. It has a curb weight of 1,742 pounds (790 kg), and it translates to 380 brake horsepower (385 ps/283 kW) per metric ton. That’s roughly similar to the Lamborghini Gallardo LP 570-4 Spyder Performante and the Ferrari 458 Italia .\nZenos says that “ all significant weight ” is “ inboard of both front and rear axles, ” and this includes the engine and gearbox. The new E10 features a fully independent front suspension with pushrod and inboard-mounted dampers for reduced drag. Both engines are turbocharged, have new induction and chargecooler packages, and are connected to a six-speed manual transmission for more driving engagement.\nConventional coil over dampers are found at the rear, mounted to the aluminum subframe that holds the engine and gearbox. There is also a limited-slip differential for enhanced traction at high-speed cornering, and the revised gear linkage mechanism is said to allow for quicker and more precise gear shifts.\nPhoto: Zenos The new Zenos E10 sports new headlights, as well as new ducting for better cooling of the front brakes, as well as revised radiator packs. The side skirts have also been upgraded for improved aerodynamics. The changes continue on the inside, where a new dashboard panel is on deck, complete with a fresh driver display, and the automaker also mentions the weatherproof switchgear, the new, in-house-made carbon fiber seats offered as standard, and a few other bits and bobs.\nThe car is offered with a full windscreen and wipers, or a race wind deflector panel. The stopping power is supplied by the uprated brakes, with new larger rotors, hugged by the four-piston calipers and brake pads every time the driver pressed the middle peddle. There is a master cylinder on deck, too, and Zenos says the stopping power and pedal feel have been significantly improved over the old E10.\nInterested parties can order the new 2027 Zenos E10 in Midnight Black, Volcano Red, Nitro Blue, Race White, Screaming Green, and Firebust Yellow exterior paint finishes, and they can also opt for a bespoke color for more customization. Both the rZ and the r2 versions rides on 16-inch front and 17-inch rear alloys, shod in 195/50 and 225/45 tires, respectively, and to absolutely no one’s surprise, they are rear-wheel drive.\nBut how much does the 2027 Zenos E10 cost? In the United Kingdom, you are looking at a minimum of 115,900 GBP for the E10 rZ, according to the company, which translates to $153,420 at today’s exchange rate. Quite surprisingly, the less powerful 2027 E10 r2 is actually more expensive, as pricing in this case kicks off at 129,900 GBP ($171,955).\nSo, is the new Zenos E10 something you’d consider buying? Let us know your thoughts about this model in the comments area below.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nZenos E10 Zenos E10 2027 zenos e10 new cars prices UK\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Cristian Gnaticov\nAfter a series of unfortunate events put an end to Cristian's dream of entering a custom built & tuned old-school Dacia into a rally competition, he moved on to drive press cars and write for a living. He's worked for several automotive online journals and now he's back at autoevolution after his first tour in the mid-2000s. Full profile\nUP NEXT Kawasaki Floods the American Market With Tens of Returning Street Motorcycles of All Shapes and Size",
